  "contracts": [
    "All25 pinned Native bodies contain zero CALL instructions.20 current C bodies are unchanged;5 work-finder interfaces reuse the established loop with actual live building/walker inputs instead of precalculated phase/type scalars.",
    "Each work-finder snapshots building DWORD58 once. For each descriptor it reads the spot pointer, checks WORD12 and descriptor phase, then loads the actual actor type BYTE, compares required type and reads work DWORD0C. Volatile actor-byte access prevents caching that live read before the gates. Actual assignment-table bounds are unchanged.",
    "Free-spot predicates use their actual type/phase inputs and expose logical AL. Finder success returns the actual input building ID in full EAX. No fabricated EAX/frame input is added.",
    "41FD80 is ECX=this plus one stack walker ID and RET4. The C algorithm stores WORD12 before the nonzero-ID gate and copies actor action BYTE to object14. MCP has no calling-convention setter; only an explanatory annotation is applied to that Native method.",
    "New small descriptor/entrance/layout structs are normalized views unless their Native offsets are explicitly identified. Clean building view7999D8 stride264 and actor viewBCD5F8 stride388 establish phase58/type0A/action38; pointer units and padding are not inferred from load width alone.",
    "Pyramid segment and pair searches keep original sentinels, style5 versus regular strides20/78, first-match ordering and second-side publication. Real Native tables/frontier lists remain caller-owned data.",
    "Menu/entrance/library/Caesareum/lighthouse/obelisk coordinate and assignment queries reuse the existing C and prior REA/Ghidra field evidence. No original-code token, IL wrapper, placeholder callback or invented lookup data is introduced.",
    "Native producer-valid coordinates/records/tables remain required. Unseen indirect consumers, actual host bindings and joint Native/C comparison remain incomplete."
  ],
